## Before you deploy: set your domain

Three files contain the placeholder `REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-DOMAIN`. Swap it for
your real address (for example `jasonlin.dev` or
`jlin82752.github.io/hopes-door-portfolio`) once you know it:

| File | What it affects |
| --- | --- |
| `index.html` | The canonical URL and the link preview card |
| `robots.txt` | The sitemap pointer |
| `sitemap.xml` | The page's listed address |

Quickest way, on macOS or Linux:

```bash
grep -rl 'REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-DOMAIN' . | xargs sed -i '' 's|REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-DOMAIN|your-domain.com|g'
```

On Linux, drop the empty `''` after `-i`.

This only matters for link previews and search engines. **The page itself works
fine without it**, so if you want to deploy first and fix the domain after, that
is a reasonable order.

