## Deploy

Pick one. All four are free for a page this size.

### Option 1 · GitHub Pages (free, no account beyond GitHub)

A workflow is already included at `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`, so every push
to `main` republishes the site automatically.

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Add portfolio"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/hopes-door-portfolio.git
git push -u origin main
```

Then, in the repository on github.com: **Settings → Pages → Source → GitHub
Actions**. The first deploy runs within a minute or two, and the URL appears on
that same Settings page.

Your address will be `https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/hopes-door-portfolio/`.

### Option 2 · Netlify (easiest, drag and drop)

Go to <https://app.netlify.com/drop> and drag this whole folder onto the page.
The site is live in seconds at a random address you can rename.

Or from the terminal:

```bash
npm run deploy:netlify
```

### Option 3 · Vercel

```bash
npm run deploy:vercel
```

Answer the prompts, accepting the defaults. It detects a static site on its own.

### Option 4 · Cloudflare Pages

In the Cloudflare dashboard: **Workers & Pages → Create → Pages → Upload
assets**, then drag the folder in. Leave the build command empty and set the
output directory to `/`.

